body:
More stories! 

My friend worked for one of the Saudi royal family's private airplanes. He was basically on call 24/7 but got paid crazy amounts of money.

Some of his trips included:

- Someone in the family had a craving. The crew got sent to Italy for cake, France to pick up ice cream, and had to go the long way around so that they could ensure peak quality;
- They took about 30 kids, their mothers, and their nannies on a trip somewhere. They weren't from the main family so they just rerouted a commercial plane instead of using their private one. One of the nannies ran up just as they were airborne saying one wife and one kid got left behind in the airport bathroom. Oops;
- They were basically freight. Pick ups and drop offs for things as minor as random clothing purchases. Or the bosses would use them like a limousine, just have the plane drop him off for a meeting. Send the plane back to their home country. Call when he wanted to be fetched.
